WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
For the first time in history,

00:02.000 --> 00:06.000
you can own your most precious cells forever.

00:06.000 --> 00:08.000
Introducing Reservoir,

00:08.000 --> 00:11.000
the world's first way for you

00:11.000 --> 00:14.000
to preserve your healthiest cells for the future.

00:14.000 --> 00:17.000
We're backed by over $120 million in funding,

00:17.000 --> 00:20.000
and our team of Harvard and MIT nerds

00:20.000 --> 00:23.000
has spent nine years developing the technology

00:23.000 --> 00:25.000
behind personalized cell medicine.

00:25.000 --> 00:27.000
We don't know what the future holds,

00:27.000 --> 00:31.000
but medical science is advancing faster than ever.

00:31.000 --> 00:32.000
We built Reservoir,

00:32.000 --> 00:35.000
so you're prepared for whatever comes next.

00:35.000 --> 00:38.000
Because the reality is, your cells deteriorate every day,

00:38.000 --> 00:40.000
which means right now,

00:40.000 --> 00:43.000
today is the youngest and healthiest they will ever be.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.000
Preserving your cells has always been limited to the ultra-wealthy.

00:47.000 --> 00:49.000
Now, it's available to anyone.

00:49.000 --> 00:51.000
Here's what actually happens.

00:51.000 --> 00:54.000
Right now, this member is going for a standard blood draw.

00:54.000 --> 00:56.000
Next, we'll isolate their immune cells

00:56.000 --> 00:59.000
and cool them to minus 150 degrees Celsius,

00:59.000 --> 01:01.000
so their cells stay frozen in time.

01:01.000 --> 01:04.000
Then they're stored in a FDA-registered facility

01:04.000 --> 01:06.000
where they wait for the future.

01:06.000 --> 01:08.000
Your cells and your data belong to you.

01:08.000 --> 01:12.000
And with Reservoir, you decide who can access it,

01:12.000 --> 01:14.000
how it's used, and for how long.

01:14.000 --> 01:16.000
Look, preserving cells isn't a new idea.

01:16.000 --> 01:20.000
Cord blood banking and egg freezing has done this for ages.

01:20.000 --> 01:22.000
But cord blood can only be collected at birth,

01:22.000 --> 01:25.000
and egg freezing requires weeks of hormone injections,

01:25.000 --> 01:28.000
a surgery, and it's a narrow window of time.

01:28.000 --> 01:31.000
With Reservoir, all it takes is one simple blood draw,

01:31.000 --> 01:33.000
and you can do it at any point in time.

01:33.000 --> 01:37.000
My whole career, I've backed people who saw the science

01:37.000 --> 01:39.000
years before the rest.

01:39.000 --> 01:41.000
This is one of those moments.

01:41.000 --> 01:43.000
I'm putting my cells in Reservoir.

01:43.000 --> 01:44.000
And you can too.

01:44.000 --> 01:46.000
The field is moving,

01:46.000 --> 01:48.000
and the youngest cells you'll ever have

01:48.000 --> 01:50.000
are the ones in your body right now.
